Scriptname FL_Wound extends ActiveMagicEffect
{Flense -- the deliberate wound.

 FleshCore's baseline is damage: hitting a body takes flesh off it, driven
 entirely inside the DLL. This spell exists so a wound can also be opened on
 purpose, at a chosen target, which is the only way to test the system without
 a fight and the only way to take a body apart at will.

 The script itself does almost nothing but decide whether this target is one
 FleshCore handles, and take away the protection that would otherwise let them
 shrug the whole thing off in silence. The wound itself is opened inside the
 DLL, off the magic-effect event, and the pieces are placed by FL_Watch.}

FormList Property Pool = None Auto
{The same twenty chunk Activators FL_Watch places from. Held here too so a
 deliberate cast does not have to wait for the watcher's next tick.}

Armor Property Interior = None Auto
{Their flesh layers, KEPT ONLY AS A FALLBACK AND NO LONGER EQUIPPED FROM HERE.

 This mattered when a body was a hollow bag and the meat had to be hung inside
 it. Now the muscle and bone are a field of closed lumps baked into
 the female and HIMBO body, hands and feet meshes, so every target is already
 solid before anything is equipped -- the engine log says so on every cast:
 "20 shape(s) (8 interior layer(s), SOLID)", and all eight of those come with
 their body.

 Equipping anyway was not free. An equip rebuilds their biped from the source
 meshes, which throws away the lattice the DLL has just built and forces it to
 read two hundred thousand vertices again on the next blow. It was paying the
 single most expensive thing this mod does, twice, for nothing.

 The DLL still asks for dressing -- by name, in FleshCore.dress.txt -- when it
 meets a body that has no fill at all, and FL_Watch still answers that. So
 the fallback survives; only the unconditional equip is gone.}

Event OnEffectStart(Actor akTarget, Actor akCaster)
    If !akTarget
        Return
    EndIf
    If !CoreActive()
        Debug.Notification("[FleshCore] engine not armed")
        Return
    EndIf
    If !Targetable(akTarget)
        Debug.Notification("[FleshCore] no effect on this target")
        Return
    EndIf
    ClearProtection(akTarget)
    ; NOTHING IS EQUIPPED HERE ANY MORE -- see the Interior property above.
    ; They are already solid, and the equip was costing their lattice.
    ;
    ; AND NOTHING IS PLACED HERE ANY MORE EITHER, WHICH IS THE POINT.
    ;
    ; This used to poll the mailbox itself and place its own wound's pieces, on
    ; the theory that a deliberate cast should not wait for the watcher's tick.
    ; What it actually bought was a second reader of a file that a third party
    ; was appending to and that both readers truncated -- so a wound landing in
    ; the wrong tenth of a second was erased before anyone placed it, and once
    ; the watcher started winning the race, wounds stopped producing pieces at
    ; all. That explains why, after the first set of pieces dropped, none
    ; dropped for anyone else.
    ;
    ; The engine now writes one file per wound, named by its own sequence, and
    ; FL_Watch claims each number exactly once. One reader, no truncation, no
    ; race -- and the watcher's tick is a twentieth of a second, which is shorter
    ; than the poll this used to do before its first look anyway. The spell's
    ; job ends where the engine's begins.
EndEvent

Bool Function CoreActive() Global
    {True only once the DLL has validated its own form lookups against the
     live form table. It deletes this file on every startup, so a stale file
     can never claim an engine that is not there.}
    Return MiscUtil.FileExists("Data/SKSE/Plugins/FleshCore.active.txt")
EndFunction

Bool Function Targetable(Actor akActor) Global
    {Whether FleshCore takes this actor: WhyRefused returns 0 -- every playable
     race, the adult vampire races of Skyrim.esm and the Afflicted, never a
     child, and either sex: the male body, hands and feet (HIMBO) carry the same
     fill as the female ones, built by the same pipeline.}
    If !akActor
        Return false
    EndIf
    ; ---- ASK THE ACTOR THEY ARE, NOT THE TEMPLATE THEY WERE STAMPED FROM -----
    ;
    ; GetActorBase returns the EDITOR base. For a levelled or dynamically
    ; spawned NPC that is the template, not the target standing there, and
    ; Actor.psc says so beside the other one: "Obtains a levelled actor's 'fake'
    ; base (the one generated by the game when the actor is levelled. This
    ; differs from GetActorBase which will return the editor base object)".
    ;
    ; MEASURED by FL_Probe: a templated NPC the engine keeps asking
    ; to have dressed can come back race='Fox' sex=0 through GetActorBase
    ; while visibly
    ; human and voxelised and wounded by the DLL without
    ; complaint. Reading the editor base refuses them on the template's race and the
    ; template's sex, so they can never be dressed at all; and because the
    ; DLL keeps a target on its pending list until their fill is real, they sit
    ; there for the rest of the session. That list holds 32 names and drops its
    ; oldest to make room, so names that can never be served push out ones that
    ; can.
    ;
    ; The levelled base first, the editor base only as a fallback for actors
    ; that have none -- which is every hand-placed NPC, where the two agree.
    ActorBase ab = akActor.GetLeveledActorBase()
    If !ab
        ab = akActor.GetActorBase()
    EndIf
    If !ab
        Return false
    EndIf
    Return WhyRefused(akActor) == 0
EndFunction

; ---- THE SAME QUESTION, WITH THE REASON KEPT ------------------------------
; 0 accepted. 1 no actor or no base record. 3 the record names no sex (GetSex()
; is -1 "None", 0 male, 1 female; both sexes are targets). 2 a race FleshCore
; does not cut, or a child; on a 2 FL_Watch writes them to FleshCore.refused.txt
; and the DLL refuses them for the session (a 3 may only be a placeholder record,
; so it is not written). Cut: every playable race, and the twelve Skyrim.esm
; races tested below (load index 00, so GetFormID is the local id): the vampire
; races Argonian, Breton, Dark Elf, High Elf, Imperial, Khajiit, Nord, Orc,
; Redguard, Wood Elf and elder, then the Afflicted. Every other non-playable race
; is refused: ElderRace, the Dremora, creatures. Never a child, whatever the race:
; IsChild(), the race's child flag (IsChildRace), "Child" in its EditorID
; (StringUtil.Find ignores case), or a child voice type on the base the sex is
; read from, which finds a child built on an adult race: MaleChild 0x00013AE8 or
; FemaleChild 0x00013AE9, the only child voices in Skyrim.esm and its DLCs. Voice
; types from other plugins are not tested: their ids move with the load order and
; nothing in their records marks a child. Argonians and Khajiit pass; their head
; fill is FL_Watch.SeatHead's call. THE ACTOR'S RACE, NOT THE RECORD'S: on a
; templated NPC, ActorBase.GetRace() can be a placeholder (FoxRace 0x00109C7C,
; their real race in the TPLT chain); Actor.GetRace() is the race after templates.
Int Function WhyRefused(Actor akActor) Global
    If !akActor
        Return 1
    EndIf
    ActorBase ab = akActor.GetLeveledActorBase()
    If !ab
        ab = akActor.GetActorBase()
    EndIf
    If !ab
        Return 1
    EndIf
    Race r = akActor.GetRace()
    If !r
        r = ab.GetRace()
    EndIf
    If !r
        Return 2
    ElseIf !r.IsPlayable()
        Int id = r.GetFormID()
        If id != 0x0008883A && id != 0x0008883C && id != 0x0008883D && id != 0x00088840 \
                && id != 0x00088844 && id != 0x00088845 && id != 0x00088794 && id != 0x000A82B9 \
                && id != 0x00088846 && id != 0x00088884 && id != 0x000A82BA && id != 0x00097A3D
            Return 2
        EndIf
    EndIf
    If akActor.IsChild() || r.IsChildRace() \
            || StringUtil.Find(PO3_SKSEFunctions.GetFormEditorID(r), "Child") >= 0
        Return 2
    EndIf
    VoiceType voice = ab.GetVoiceType()
    If voice
        Int voiceId = voice.GetFormID()
        If voiceId == 0x00013AE8 || voiceId == 0x00013AE9
            Return 2
        EndIf
    EndIf
    If ab.GetSex() < 0
        Return 3
    EndIf
    Return 0
EndFunction

Function ClearProtection(Actor akActor) Global
    {Protected and Essential actors survive everything in silence, which reads
     as the spell being broken. Both flags are cleared on the target's own base
     so the body can actually come apart.}
    ActorBase ab = akActor.GetActorBase()
    If ab
        ab.SetProtected(false)
        ab.SetEssential(false)
    EndIf
EndFunction
